<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vicente Cerna y Cerna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1815">1815</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vicente Cerna y Cerna (1815–1885) was a Guatemalan general and conservative politician who succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-carrera">Rafael Carrera</a> as president in 1865. He continued Carrera's alliance with the church and the conservative elite but faced growing liberal opposition, and he was overthrown in 1871 by the Liberal Revolution led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-garcia-granados">Miguel García Granados</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justo-rufino-barrios">Justo Rufino Barrios</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vicente-cerna-y-cerna.jpg" alt="Vicente Cerna y Cerna" width="240" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Presidencia de Guatemala · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VicenteCerna_(oficial).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Liberal Revolution of 1871, led by Miguel García Granados and Justo Rufino Barrios, overthrew Carrera’s successor <b>Vicente Cerna</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala">Republic of Guatemala · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Jutiapa, in what is now <a href="/countries/guatemala">Guatemala</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala-city">Guatemala City</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/guatemala">Guatemala</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=14.28,-89.89&amp;year=1860" aria-label="Jutiapa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2090 1632 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Vicente Cerna y Cerna"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2540 1902h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2540 1902h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=14.28,-89.89&amp;year=1860">What was here in 1860? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
